No marriage license for John and Annie has been located despite extensive search.

Several lines of evidence nonetheless establish the marriage. The couple lived as man and wife, and the 1880 census records them as a married couple in the same household. Most significantly, John himself cited this marriage date and a marriage location on his later divorce filing — a strong piece of self-reported evidence from the party with the most direct knowledge.

Annie E. Chaney is Shannon Field's 2x great-grandmother. Following the divorce, finalized 14 September 1899, Annie remarried. She had no further children and died in 1932.

**Open question:** the absence of a marriage license is notable given the marriage's apparent duration. Possible explanations include an unrecorded ceremony, a license recorded in a jurisdiction not yet searched, or loss/damage to the original record. This remains worth pursuing.